  <Docs>
    <summary>Provides the utterance identifier for a .NET handler of the legacy utterance-completion callback.</summary>
    <remarks>
      <para>The legacy <see cref="T:Android.Speech.Tts.TextToSpeech.IOnUtteranceCompletedListener" /> callback is made only for an utterance that has an identifier. It does not distinguish successful completion from an error or stop. Use <see cref="T:Android.Speech.Tts.UtteranceProgressListener" /> for progress and error notifications. This event data stores an identifier; it does not contain a success or error status.</para>
      <para><format type="text/html"><a href="https://android.googlesource.com/platform/frameworks/base/+/1cdfff555f4a21f71ccc978290e2e212e2f8b168/core/java/android/speech/tts/UtteranceProgressListener.java">Android adapter for the legacy completion callback.</a> <a href="https://github.com/dotnet/java-interop/blob/92b5d471f1e0f6164fc332b1f661b472f5cf3aad/tools/generator/SourceWriters/InterfaceEventArgsClass.cs">.NET event argument storage implementation.</a></format></para>
      <para>Portions of this page are modifications based on work created and shared by the <format type="text/html"><a href="https://developers.google.com/terms/site-policies" title="Android Open Source Project">Android Open Source Project</a></format> and used according to terms described in the <format type="text/html"><a href="https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by/2.5/" title="Creative Commons 2.5 Attribution License">Creative Commons 2.5 Attribution License.</a></format></para>
    </remarks>
  </Docs>
